      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good start, but looking at the draft, I'm a bit worried. It's starting to feel a little repetitive in certain spots—like that bit about \"the citizen\" in the second paragraph feels slightly clunky. \n\nThat said, I just ran a test check through the tracker and the score is actually lower than I was hoping for. We really need to hit a higher threshold to get past the auto-filter. \n\nCan you do another pass on this? Try to find more ways to integrate the term so the score increases significantly. I'm still really emphasizing that we can't have it look like a list of keywords—it has to look like a professional urban planner wrote it—but we definitely need to nudge that \"citizen\" count up a bit more to ensure we don't get filtered out.",
